   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Cut the region into thin sectors by rays from the pole. A sector of radius r and small angle \\( \\Delta\\theta \\) has area \\( \\frac{1}{2} r^{2} \\Delta\\theta \\), the fraction \\( \\frac{\\Delta\\theta}{2\\pi} \\) of the disc of area \\( \\pi r^{2} \\).",
         "rule_named": "area of a circular sector"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Adding the sectors and letting the angles shrink turns the sum into an integral over the angles the region sweeps, so the area is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\int_{0}^{2 \\pi} \\left(12 - 9 \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}\\,d\\theta \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99048",
         "rule_named": "polar area integral"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluating the integral gives \\( \\frac{369 \\pi}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Rational",
               369,
               2
            ],
            "Pi"
         ],
         "rule_named": "definite integral evaluated"
      }
   ],
